5
00:00:13,060 --> 00:00:19,920
They basically invited all the world's most prestigious scientists to London to witness this demonstration at a museum.

6
00:00:20,520 --> 00:00:23,700
And the claim was that they had built this machine called Orbo.

7
00:00:23,980 --> 00:00:25,360
Right, the infamous Orbo.

8
00:00:25,360 --> 00:00:29,380
Yeah, and they claimed it produced free, limitless energy.

9
00:00:30,040 --> 00:00:36,240
Like, they were essentially promising to rewrite the fundamental laws of thermodynamics right there on a public stage.

10
00:00:36,320 --> 00:00:37,600
It was incredibly bold.

11
00:00:37,720 --> 00:00:38,200
Super bold.

12
00:00:38,420 --> 00:00:43,660
So the cameras are rolling, the scientific jury is seated, the anticipation in the room is just, you know, electric.

13
00:00:43,840 --> 00:00:47,200
And then, live on stage, the machine just sat there.

14
00:00:47,240 --> 00:00:48,400
Just a heavy paperweight.

15
00:00:48,660 --> 00:00:50,220
Literally did absolutely nothing.

16
00:00:50,320 --> 00:00:51,480
The whole thing failed completely.

17
00:00:51,480 --> 00:00:55,040
I think they blamed the heat from the stage lights or something.

18
00:00:55,180 --> 00:00:58,420
Yeah, thermal expansion of the bearings, which is a classic excuse.

19
00:00:58,700 --> 00:00:58,880
Right.

20
00:00:59,380 --> 00:01:11,840
And so the scientific jury eventually issued this very polite but unanimous verdict that basically said, you know, there is zero evidence of anomalous energy production happening here.

21
00:01:11,960 --> 00:01:17,440
It was just one of the most spectacular, highly funded scientific embarrassments of the 21st century.

22
00:01:17,440 --> 00:01:23,440
It really is the ultimate cautionary tale because, you know, the people who built that machine, they weren't just running a conscious scam.

23
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:24,840
You don't think so?

24
00:01:24,980 --> 00:01:25,240
No.

25
00:01:25,380 --> 00:01:28,340
I mean, they genuinely believed they had cracked the code of the universe.

26
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:34,220
They believed in it enough to risk total public humiliation in front of the entire scientific establishment.

27
00:01:34,220 --> 00:01:42,020
And that profound disconnect, right, between absolute certainty and physical reality, that is exactly where we are heading today.

