00:02:51,500 --> 00:02:52,100
So settle in.

47
00:02:52,160 --> 00:03:01,160
We promise you a shortcut to becoming insanely well-informed on everything from Nikola Tesla's supposed death ray to the hardcore physics of why you literally cannot walk through walls.

48
00:03:01,240 --> 00:03:09,260
So to understand these grand sweeping claims about zero-point energy or alien technology, we actually have to start incredibly small.

49
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:10,560
Like garage-level small.

50
00:03:10,560 --> 00:03:11,460
Exactly.

51
00:03:11,700 --> 00:03:15,920
We have to look at the wires, the dials, and the multimeters on a workbench.

52
00:03:16,500 --> 00:03:23,180
Because the deepest, most complex rabbit holes almost always start with a very human, very mundane error.

53
00:03:23,960 --> 00:03:24,980
A misread gauge.

54
00:03:25,240 --> 00:03:29,160
I love this part because we just assume tools are completely objective.

55
00:03:29,320 --> 00:03:34,560
Like a multimeter gives you a crisp digital readout, so it must be the absolute truth.

56
00:03:34,660 --> 00:03:34,840
Right.

57
00:03:34,960 --> 00:03:36,800
It's got numbers on a screen, so it's math.

58
00:03:36,800 --> 00:03:37,440
Exactly.

59
00:03:37,880 --> 00:03:44,920
So let's look at this classic example that has dominated hobbyist free energy forums since, like, the 1980s.

60
00:03:45,420 --> 00:03:46,240
The Bedini motor.

61
00:03:46,440 --> 00:03:46,780
Oh, yeah.

62
00:03:46,900 --> 00:03:47,440
John Bedini.

63
00:03:47,580 --> 00:03:47,780
Right.

64
00:03:48,020 --> 00:03:55,100
He claimed you could use a pulsed switching circuit to charge a secondary battery using less energy than that secondary battery ends up storing.

65
00:03:55,480 --> 00:04:00,200
So the idea is you run the motor, you swap the batteries back and forth, and boom, eventually you have infinite power.

66
00:04:00,200 --> 00:04:12,900
Which sounds great until you actually look at how batteries work, because the illusion of free energy with the Bedini setup stems almost entirely from a fundamental misunderstanding of battery chemistry, and specifically how you measure it.

67
00:04:12,960 --> 00:04:14,120
Okay, break that down for us.

68
00:04:14,420 --> 00:04:20,120
So when a builder tests this setup, they usually look at the primary battery's coarse voltage sag.

69
00:04:20,640 --> 00:04:26,240
That is, how much the voltage drops while it is actively under the load of running the motor.

70
00:04:26,380 --> 00:04:28,160
Right, it's working hard, so the voltage dips.

71
00:04:28,160 --> 00:04:38,580
Yes. Then they compare that to the secondary battery's open-circuit voltage recovery after it gets hit with a series of very rapid, high-voltage, pulsed charges.

72
00:04:38,920 --> 00:04:45,320
So to put this in everyday terms for you listening, imagine you are driving a car up a really steep hill.

73
00:04:45,600 --> 00:04:46,460
Okay, good analogy.

74
00:04:46,720 --> 00:04:51,040
The fuel gauge might momentarily slosh backward, or the engine temperature spikes.

75
00:04:51,180 --> 00:04:51,400
Mm-hmm.

76
00:04:51,580 --> 00:04:54,120
You are basically taking a reading under extreme duress.

77
00:04:54,260 --> 00:04:54,500
Right.

78
00:04:54,500 --> 00:04:58,480
But then you park the car, you let it sit, and the gauges settle back to normal.

79
00:04:59,180 --> 00:05:07,920
If you compare the stressed reading to the rested reading, you might actually trick yourself into thinking the car miraculously generated its own fluids while it was parked.

80
00:05:08,300 --> 00:05:10,100
That captures the dynamic perfectly.

81
00:05:10,520 --> 00:05:19,680
A battery's terminal voltage, which is just the number you see on a basic multimeter, well, it recovers much faster than its actual internal chemical state of charge.

82
00:05:19,680 --> 00:05:22,560
So it looks full, but it's not actually full.

83
00:05:22,900 --> 00:05:23,440
Exactly.

84
00:05:23,720 --> 00:05:28,820
And this is especially true when you are slamming the battery with short, sharp spikes of current.

85
00:05:29,100 --> 00:05:36,460
A standard voltmeter looks at that high-voltage pulse, sees the resting voltage bounce up, and it looks like a miracle.

86
00:05:36,660 --> 00:05:37,720
But it's just surface level.

87
00:05:37,720 --> 00:05:52,000
Completely, because if you put that exact same Bedini circuit through a rigorous calorimetric test, where you basically enclose the battery in an insulated water bath and measure the actual physical heat dissipated, the math changes.

88
00:05:52,420 --> 00:05:55,560
Or if you just carefully integrate the current over a long time, right?

89
00:05:55,560 --> 00:06:01,160
Yes. If you do either of those things, the so-called extra energy completely vanishes.

90
00:06:01,600 --> 00:06:06,320
The overunity is just an artifact of how pulsed charging tricks a simple voltmeter.

91
00:06:06,580 --> 00:06:08,680
It is absolutely not new physics.

92
00:06:08,840 --> 00:06:15,040
And that specific trap, the whole pulsed waveform tricking a standard meter thing, it is everywhere in these fringe communities.

93
00:06:15,180 --> 00:06:18,300
Like, it is the beating heart of Stanley Meyer's famous water fuel cell.

94
00:06:18,340 --> 00:06:19,600
Oh, the dune buggy guy.

95
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:30,820
Yes. Meyer claimed he could split water into hydrogen and oxygen using just a tiny fraction of the energy it conventionally takes, and then use that gas to run a literal dune buggy.

96
00:06:31,520 --> 00:06:36,380
And Philip Kanarev made really similar claims about this hyper-efficient electrolysis.

97
00:06:36,500 --> 00:06:39,240
But we really need to anchor this in thermodynamic reality.

98
00:06:40,180 --> 00:06:46,880
Splitting one mole of water into hydrogen and oxygen requires a fixed thermodynamic cost.

99
00:06:46,880 --> 00:06:50,020
It's roughly 286 kilojoules.

100
00:06:50,300 --> 00:06:51,800
And that's just a rule of the universe.

101
00:06:52,140 --> 00:06:56,840
It is a hard chemical boundary dictated by the actual strength of the molecular bonds.

102
00:06:57,280 --> 00:06:59,200
Water molecules do not negotiate.

103
00:06:59,520 --> 00:07:01,300
I love that. They do not negotiate.

104
00:07:01,480 --> 00:07:06,960
They don't. It does not matter how clever your circuit is or how you shape the electrical pulse hitting the water.

105
00:07:07,080 --> 00:07:08,280
You have to pay the toll.

106
00:07:08,620 --> 00:07:12,720
But Meyer's whole defense, right, was that he wasn't using brute force direct current.

107
00:07:12,720 --> 00:07:18,980
He claimed he was using what he called resonant pulses to somehow shatter the water molecule at its natural frequency.

108
00:07:19,220 --> 00:07:21,940
Right, trying to bypass that 286 kilojoule limit.

109
00:07:22,140 --> 00:07:22,520
Exactly.

110
00:07:22,840 --> 00:07:23,000
Yeah.

111
00:07:23,040 --> 00:07:25,320
And he had the gauges to prove his input power was tiny.

112
00:07:26,100 --> 00:07:33,140
He even took this all to court in 1996, though, spoiler alert, he was ultimately found guilty of gross and egregious fraud.

113
00:07:33,360 --> 00:07:33,560
Yeah.

114
00:07:34,280 --> 00:07:37,840
But how did his instruments lie to him so convincingly in the first place?

115
00:07:37,960 --> 00:07:40,980
Well, it comes down to metrology, which is the science of measurement.

116
00:07:40,980 --> 00:07:47,780
When you generate a highly complex, non-sinusoidal pulsed waveform, like a sharp needle pulse of voltage,

117
00:07:48,020 --> 00:07:54,060
you cannot measure the power it delivers with just a standard, average-reading multimeter from the hardware store.

118
00:07:54,240 --> 00:07:58,540
I actually want to pause here for a second because I think most people, including myself until very recently,

119
00:07:58,660 --> 00:08:01,880
assume a voltmeter just, you know, counts the electrons passing through.

120
00:08:02,460 --> 00:08:04,520
Why does the shape of the pulse break the meter?

121
00:08:04,520 --> 00:08:11,840
So most off-the-shelf multimeters are designed to read standard alternating current, like what comes directly out of your wall socket.

122
00:08:12,060 --> 00:08:12,200
Okay.

123
00:08:12,420 --> 00:08:15,520
And a wall socket provides a smooth, continuous sine wave.

124
00:08:15,900 --> 00:08:20,980
To give you a readable number on the screen, a cheap meter just assumes the wave is a perfect sine shape,

125
00:08:21,380 --> 00:08:26,600
it measures the peak, and it multiplies it by roughly 1707 to give you an average.

126
00:08:26,600 --> 00:08:27,840
Oh, so it's doing a mass shortcut.

127
00:08:28,240 --> 00:08:29,140
Yes, exactly.

128
00:08:29,640 --> 00:08:32,540
But Stanley Meyer wasn't using smooth waves.

129
00:08:32,780 --> 00:08:36,940
He was using sharp, jagged spikes with these long pauses in between.

130
00:08:37,700 --> 00:08:42,240
When you feed a sharp needle pulse into a meter that's expecting a smooth rolling wave,

131
00:08:42,760 --> 00:08:45,820
the meter's internal math completely breaks down.

132
00:08:45,900 --> 00:08:47,220
It just doesn't know what to do with it.

133
00:08:47,280 --> 00:08:47,520
Right.

134
00:08:47,620 --> 00:08:50,520
It vastly underestimates the total area under the curve.

135
00:08:50,520 --> 00:08:57,900
To measure a complex pulse, you need specialized equipment that calculates the true root-mean-square, or RMS, power.

136
00:08:58,080 --> 00:09:00,620
And I'm guessing Meyer didn't use an RMS oscilloscope.

137
00:09:00,780 --> 00:09:01,780
He did not.

138
00:09:02,200 --> 00:09:08,980
But when electrical engineers finally analyzed Meyer's cells and Karnarov's cells using proper RMS oscilloscopes,

139
00:09:09,200 --> 00:09:11,240
the illusion shattered entirely.

140
00:09:11,620 --> 00:09:16,360
The actual power being delivered by those sharp spikes perfectly matched standard thermodynamics.

141
00:09:16,360 --> 00:09:21,340
The revolutionary efficiency was literally just a math error inside a cheap tool.

142
00:09:21,600 --> 00:09:22,600
That is just wild.

143
00:09:22,720 --> 00:09:26,060
You can build a decades-long mythology off an uncalibrated tool.

144
00:09:26,200 --> 00:09:27,780
It happens more often than you'd think.

145
00:09:27,860 --> 00:09:28,420
I believe it.

146
00:09:28,660 --> 00:09:31,720
But we also see a totally different flavor of this with mechanical generators,

147
00:09:32,240 --> 00:09:36,620
like Paramahans-Otori's space power generator, or Bustapalma's end machine.

148
00:09:36,960 --> 00:09:38,360
Right, the homopolar generator.

149
00:09:38,460 --> 00:09:41,340
Yeah, these were massive, spinning metal disks,

150
00:09:41,340 --> 00:09:49,180
and they claimed the generator was outputting way more electrical power than it actually took to physically spin the shaft.

151
00:09:49,300 --> 00:09:54,820
Which introduces a critical error in mechanical testing known as the motor input proxy.

152
00:09:55,020 --> 00:09:55,900
Motor input proxy.

153
00:09:56,100 --> 00:09:56,940
Okay, what is that?

154
00:09:57,120 --> 00:10:00,480
Well, if you want to scientifically measure the efficiency of a generator,

155
00:10:00,860 --> 00:10:04,800
you have to measure exactly how much mechanical energy is being put into it.

156
00:10:04,800 --> 00:10:11,300
The rigorous way to do this is to install a physical torque sensor directly on the rotating shaft

157
00:10:11,300 --> 00:10:14,020
that connects the driving motor to the generator.

158
00:10:14,420 --> 00:10:16,440
So you're measuring the actual twist of the metal?

159
00:10:16,580 --> 00:10:19,460
Yes, the physical twist and the speed of the metal shaft.

160
00:10:19,620 --> 00:10:24,260
And I'm guessing Tiwari and De Palma didn't bother to buy a torque sensor.

161
00:10:24,520 --> 00:10:25,140
They did not.

162
00:10:25,460 --> 00:10:30,640
Instead, they measured the electrical power going into the electric motor that was driving the generator.

163
00:10:30,640 --> 00:10:35,660
They used the motor's electrical input as a proxy for the mechanical output.

164
00:10:36,180 --> 00:10:37,600
But motors aren't 100% efficient.

165
00:10:37,860 --> 00:10:39,920
Like, they get hot, they hum, they vibrate.

166
00:10:40,340 --> 00:10:40,940
Exactly.

167
00:10:41,220 --> 00:10:43,300
Every single motor has conversion losses.

168
00:10:44,040 --> 00:10:48,240
You have friction in the bearings, heat in the copper windings, electrical resistance.

169
00:10:48,920 --> 00:10:52,600
By using the electrical input to the driving motor as their baseline,

170
00:10:53,120 --> 00:10:58,180
they systematically hid the driving motor's own inefficiency from the final equation.

171
00:10:58,440 --> 00:10:59,960
They just swept it under the rug.

172
00:10:59,960 --> 00:11:00,760
Pretty much.

173
00:11:01,340 --> 00:11:04,340
Furthermore, homopolar generators like De Palma's end machine,

174
00:11:04,340 --> 00:11:11,360
they require liquid metal or heavy physical brushes to drag against the spinning disk just to pull the current off.

175
00:11:11,640 --> 00:11:12,880
Which creates a ton of friction.

176
00:11:13,060 --> 00:11:13,760
Immense friction.

177
00:11:14,340 --> 00:11:18,720
So when independent laboratories properly accounted for the brush contact losses

178
00:11:18,720 --> 00:11:21,340
and measured the actual physical shaft torque,

179
00:11:21,880 --> 00:11:24,840
the so-called overunity disappeared instantly.

180
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:26,540
It's just a systemic blind spot.

181
00:11:26,920 --> 00:11:29,700
You are measuring the system right where you want it to look good,

182
00:11:29,700 --> 00:11:34,480
and ignoring the parts of the system that are secretly bleeding energy everywhere else.

183
00:11:34,580 --> 00:11:35,100
Exactly.

184
00:11:35,580 --> 00:11:40,280
And speaking of bleeding energy, we have to talk about Thane Hines and the Peripidia effect.

185
00:11:40,620 --> 00:11:42,760
That went super viral online a while back.

186
00:11:42,800 --> 00:11:44,220
Oh yes, the accelerating motor.

187
00:11:44,220 --> 00:11:49,280
He had these videos showing an electric motor that actually accelerated,

188
00:11:49,500 --> 00:11:56,300
like it visibly sped up when he applied a really heavy magnetic load to the generator it was driving.

189
00:11:56,540 --> 00:12:00,780
And that feels completely impossible because it violates Lenz's law, right?

190
00:12:00,940 --> 00:12:02,320
It absolutely violates it.

191
00:12:03,020 --> 00:12:05,760
Lenz's law is foundational to electromagnetism.

192
00:12:05,760 --> 00:12:14,220
It essentially states that the direction of an induced electrical current will always create a magnetic field that opposes the change that produced it.

193
00:12:14,660 --> 00:12:15,380
Okay, so in English.

194
00:12:15,940 --> 00:12:20,420
In simple terms, if you try to pull energy out of a generator, the generator pushes back.

195
00:12:20,640 --> 00:12:22,120
It creates magnetic drag.

196
00:12:22,540 --> 00:12:24,540
This isn't just a rule of thumb either.

197
00:12:24,540 --> 00:12:28,660
It is a direct, unavoidable manifestation of the conservation of energy.

198
00:12:28,820 --> 00:12:31,100
Right, because otherwise things would just spin out of control.

199
00:12:31,220 --> 00:12:31,660
Exactly.

200
00:12:32,240 --> 00:12:35,780
If induced currents reinforced a driving motor instead of opposing it,

201
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:42,120
a generator would spontaneously accelerate itself to infinite speeds, pulling infinite energy from nowhere.

202
00:12:42,500 --> 00:12:45,600
So when a video shows a motor speeding up under a heavy load,

203
00:12:45,780 --> 00:12:48,620
we have to look past the magnets and look at the motor controller.

204
00:12:49,040 --> 00:12:50,840
The speed controller's feedback loop.

205
00:12:51,040 --> 00:12:52,940
This blew my mind when I read it in the dossier.

206
00:12:52,940 --> 00:12:57,660
It is a really well-documented artifact in the engineering of motor controllers.

207
00:12:58,580 --> 00:13:03,700
When a heavy load induces a strong back electromotive force, or back EMF,

208
00:13:04,160 --> 00:13:07,920
that messy electrical noise feeds backward through the wires,

209
00:13:08,280 --> 00:13:13,580
and it can actually alter the feedback signal going to the electronic speed controller.

210
00:13:13,880 --> 00:13:15,720
So it scrambles the brain of the machine.

211
00:13:15,900 --> 00:13:16,260
Right.

212
00:13:16,540 --> 00:13:21,040
The controller's microchip gets confused by the noise, it thinks the motor is stalling out,

213
00:13:21,040 --> 00:13:28,680
and it compensates by drawing significantly more power from the wall socket to physically force the motor to spin faster.

214
00:13:29,220 --> 00:13:32,460
So on video, it looks like the magnets are creating free energy,

215
00:13:32,600 --> 00:13:36,660
but if you just looked at the wall outlet, you'd see the power cord getting incredibly hot.

216
00:13:37,020 --> 00:13:37,540
Precisely.

217
00:13:37,760 --> 00:13:41,360
If you put a simple wattmeter on the wall socket powering the whole setup,

218
00:13:41,560 --> 00:13:45,960
you would see the power draw spike massively the exact moment the motor speeds up.

219
00:13:45,960 --> 00:13:48,360
The generator isn't creating energy out of the vacuum.

220
00:13:48,780 --> 00:13:51,960
The confused controller is just electronically opening the throttle.

221
00:13:52,300 --> 00:13:53,740
It's just so simple when you break it down.

222
00:13:54,400 --> 00:13:56,240
But before we move on from flawed measurements,

223
00:13:56,480 --> 00:13:59,460
we have to talk about Bruce De Palma's spinning ball experiment.

224
00:13:59,800 --> 00:14:00,300
Classic.

225
00:14:00,640 --> 00:14:02,400
Yeah, because this wasn't an electrical trick.

226
00:14:02,480 --> 00:14:03,600
This was purely mechanical.

227
00:14:05,100 --> 00:14:09,100
De Palma took a steel ball, spun it up to incredibly high speeds,

228
00:14:09,100 --> 00:14:15,880
and then launched it upward from this spring-loaded cup alongside an identical but non-spinning ball.

229
00:14:16,420 --> 00:14:19,060
And he claimed the spinning ball went higher and fell faster,

230
00:14:19,600 --> 00:14:22,740
proving that rotation somehow alters gravitational mass.

231
00:14:22,740 --> 00:14:29,760
And this is a beautiful textbook example of a mechanical artifact being mistaken for entirely new physics.

232
00:14:30,500 --> 00:14:34,300
When you place a rapidly spinning steel ball into a stationary launch cup,

233
00:14:34,300 --> 00:14:41,380
you are introducing intense, frictional, and gyroscopic interactions during the crucial milliseconds of the launch sequence.

234
00:14:41,660 --> 00:14:44,680
It's like a tire doing a burnout against the side of the cup.

235
00:14:44,740 --> 00:14:46,780
That is a highly accurate comparison, yeah.

236
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:51,600
The spinning ball literally pushes off the inner wall of the cup differently than a stationary ball does.

237
00:14:51,760 --> 00:14:54,120
It alters the exit velocity and the trajectory.

238
00:14:54,500 --> 00:14:56,720
And let me guess, someone tested this properly.

239
00:14:57,060 --> 00:14:57,560
They did.

240
00:14:57,560 --> 00:15:03,120
When later researchers replicated this exact experiment using high-speed cameras

241
00:15:03,120 --> 00:15:08,820
and perfectly controlled magnetic release mechanisms that completely eliminated the launch cup friction,

242
00:15:09,240 --> 00:15:10,960
the effect vanished entirely.

243
00:15:11,920 --> 00:15:16,620
Gravity treats a spinning mass and a non-spinning mass with absolute equality.

244
00:15:16,860 --> 00:15:23,840
Okay, so we've established that garage-level metrology and hidden friction explain away a lot of these anomalies.

245
00:15:24,040 --> 00:15:25,460
A vast majority of them, yes.

246
00:15:25,460 --> 00:15:28,400
But what happens when the initial observation isn't a mistake?

247
00:15:29,140 --> 00:15:32,920
What happens when an inventor reads a real paper on quantum physics,

248
00:15:33,480 --> 00:15:37,300
sees a genuine phenomenon, and decides they can build a spaceship out of it?

249
00:15:37,780 --> 00:15:40,480
This is where we hit the scale blindness epidemic.

250
00:15:40,620 --> 00:15:41,720
It's a very common trap.

251
00:15:41,880 --> 00:15:44,560
Taking a genuine microscopic quantum phenomenon,

252
00:15:44,900 --> 00:15:48,840
and just assuming it works on a macroscopic human scale without doing any of the math.

253
00:15:48,960 --> 00:15:52,100
Well, the word quantum has suffered a pretty terrible fate in popular culture.

254
00:15:52,100 --> 00:15:56,520
In the realm of fringe physics, quantum functions as a linguistic wild card.

255
00:15:56,660 --> 00:15:57,700
It just means magic now.

256
00:15:57,960 --> 00:15:58,620
Essentially, yeah.

257
00:15:59,200 --> 00:16:08,840
It provides inventors with a highly technical-sounding vocabulary to just arbitrarily bypass fixed thermodynamic laws and structural mechanics.

258
00:16:08,840 --> 00:16:14,920
So let's tackle the ultimate sci-fi concept that gets thrown around in these circles, which is walking through walls.

259
00:16:15,280 --> 00:16:20,460
You hear this a lot in fringe self-improvement or quantum mysticism circles.

260
00:16:20,800 --> 00:16:22,220
And the pitch goes like this, right?

261
00:16:22,940 --> 00:16:24,860
Atoms are mostly empty space.

262
00:16:25,460 --> 00:16:28,300
We know that electrons can quantum tunnel through barriers.

263
00:16:28,300 --> 00:16:32,260
Therefore, a human being is just a collection of tunneling particles.

264
00:16:32,840 --> 00:16:37,020
And if you align your frequencies, you could technically phase through a solid brick wall.

265
00:16:37,500 --> 00:16:37,800
Right.

266
00:16:38,080 --> 00:16:42,020
To dismantle this, we first have to explain why solid matter actually feels solid.

267
00:16:42,360 --> 00:16:44,940
It is not because atoms are crowded like billiard balls.

268
00:16:45,540 --> 00:16:48,820
Matter resists interpenetration due to two fundamental forces.

269
00:16:48,900 --> 00:16:49,640
Okay, what's the first one?

270
00:16:49,640 --> 00:16:55,500
The first is electrostatic repulsion between the electron clouds of the atoms in your hand and the atoms in the wall.

271
00:16:55,700 --> 00:17:00,340
But the much stronger, truly unbreakable barrier is the Pauli exclusion principle.

272
00:17:00,740 --> 00:17:03,920
Unpack the Pauli exclusion principle for me because that sounds intense.

273
00:17:03,920 --> 00:17:11,600
It is a quantum mechanical principle stating that two identical fermions, so particles like electrons, protons, and neutrons,

274
00:17:11,780 --> 00:17:15,360
they cannot occupy the exact same quantum states simultaneously.

275
00:17:15,640 --> 00:17:17,000
They refuse to share the same seat.

276
00:17:17,440 --> 00:17:18,000
Exactly.

277
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:25,740
When you press your hand against a wall, you are forcing the electrons in your hand into the same space as the electrons in the wall.

278
00:17:26,120 --> 00:17:34,060
The universe aggressively forbids this, creating an incredibly stiff contact force called electron degeneracy pressure.

279
00:17:34,660 --> 00:17:37,040
That is what solid actually is.

280
00:17:37,140 --> 00:17:38,580
Okay, but electrons do tunnel.

281
00:17:38,920 --> 00:17:40,060
Like, that is real physics.

282
00:17:40,540 --> 00:17:43,780
Scanning tunneling microscopes literally rely on it to function.

283
00:17:43,920 --> 00:17:45,840
Oh, quantum tunneling is absolutely real.

284
00:17:45,840 --> 00:17:55,540
An electron behaving as a wave has a non-zero probability of appearing on the far side of a potential energy barrier that it classically does not have the energy to climb over.

285
00:17:55,640 --> 00:17:56,860
It just pops out on the other side.

286
00:17:56,960 --> 00:17:57,100
Right.

287
00:17:57,480 --> 00:18:02,580
However, the mathematical probability of that happening is dictated by an exponential decay equation.

288
00:18:03,360 --> 00:18:05,680
And the exponent is where the fantasy dies, doesn't it?

289
00:18:05,900 --> 00:18:07,900
The exponent is everything here.

290
00:18:07,900 --> 00:18:13,060
The probability drops exponentially based on the mass of the object and the width of the barrier.

291
00:18:13,700 --> 00:18:20,600
When you calculate the tunneling probability for a single electron across a gap of a few nanometers, it happens frequently.

292
00:18:20,720 --> 00:18:20,920
Sure.

293
00:18:21,080 --> 00:18:21,840
Microscopic scale.

294
00:18:21,840 --> 00:18:35,380
But when you substitute the mass of a single electron for the mass of an 80 kilogram human body, and you substitute a nanometer gap for the width of a standard brick wall, that exponent becomes so negative it destroys the mind.

295
00:18:35,720 --> 00:18:38,200
How small of a chance are we actually talking about here?

296
00:18:38,480 --> 00:18:47,840
The probability of a human body macroscopically tunneling through a wall has more zeros after the decimal point than there are elementary particles in the entire observable universe.

297
00:18:47,980 --> 00:18:48,760
Oh my God.

298
00:18:48,760 --> 00:18:53,380
Yeah. To call the chance vanishingly small is a comedic understatement.

299
00:18:53,900 --> 00:19:03,900
If you had trillions of humans walking into walls trillions of times a second, it is an event that would not be expected to occur across the entire remaining lifespan of the universe until the last stars burn out.

300
00:19:04,340 --> 00:19:09,280
You simply cannot scale up a subatomic probability to a macroscopic object.

301
00:19:09,720 --> 00:19:11,540
Trillions of humans hitting walls.

302
00:19:12,120 --> 00:19:15,140
But people keep trying to scale up the quantum world.

303
00:19:15,140 --> 00:19:23,020
Let's talk about zero point energy, because the Casimir effect is basically the holy grail for free energy inventors.

304
00:19:23,240 --> 00:19:24,360
It is brought up constantly.

305
00:19:24,560 --> 00:19:35,820
Right. The idea is two uncharged metal plates placed incredibly close together in a perfect vacuum will actually attract each other, seemingly pushed together by quantum fluctuations in the empty space around them.

306
00:19:35,820 --> 00:19:40,760
And the Casimir effect does prove that vacuum energy is a real physical phenomenon.

307
00:19:41,500 --> 00:19:47,220
The plates do snap together, and in doing so, they perform a tiny, microscopic amount of physical work.

308
00:19:47,480 --> 00:19:48,500
So there is energy there.

309
00:19:48,660 --> 00:19:55,320
There is. But extracting that energy in bulk to run a city, or even a toaster, is a thermodynamic nightmare.

310
00:19:55,520 --> 00:19:57,920
Because it's not just a battery you can plug into and drain.

311
00:19:57,920 --> 00:20:02,260
Precisely. The Casimir effect represents a one-time shift in boundary conditions.

312
00:20:02,520 --> 00:20:05,480
The plates snap together, releasing a minuscule amount of energy.

313
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:12,860
But to create a cyclical engine, an engine that runs continuously, you have to pull those plates back apart to reset the system.

314
00:20:12,980 --> 00:20:14,040
Oh, I see where this is going.

315
00:20:14,280 --> 00:20:20,800
Right. And pulling them apart against the vacuum pressure costs exactly as much energy as you just gain when they snap together.

316
00:20:20,920 --> 00:20:21,960
It's a zero-sum game.

317
00:20:21,960 --> 00:20:33,980
It is thermodynamically identical to saying a stretched rubber band is a source of limitless free energy because it violently snaps shut while totally ignoring the muscular energy you expended to stretch it in the first place.

318
00:20:34,140 --> 00:20:40,200
The quantum vacuum is not a reservoir of fuel. It is a state. It owes you nothing.

319
00:20:40,700 --> 00:20:43,520
The vacuum owes you nothing. That is such a great phrase.

320
00:20:43,520 --> 00:20:52,820
And we see this exact same scale blindness with the anti-gravity claims tied to cold fusion and the infamous Pays patents.

321
00:20:52,940 --> 00:20:54,160
Yes, the Navy patents.

322
00:20:54,280 --> 00:21:04,880
Salvatore Pays, working as an engineer for the U.S. Navy, patented a theoretical craft that supposedly reduced its own inertial mass by vibrating a microwave cavity at incredibly high frequencies.

323
00:21:05,640 --> 00:21:12,600
And the claim was that the intense electromagnetic fields would manipulate the local quantum vacuum and basically decouple the ship from gravity.

324
00:21:12,600 --> 00:21:16,380
This is where we really have to talk about the stale gap in general relativity.

325
00:21:16,380 --> 00:21:23,980
Let us grant, strictly for the sake of argument, that you could slightly manipulate the local vacuum energy inside a microwave cavity.

326
00:21:24,480 --> 00:21:29,320
Or even that the anomalous heat claimed by cold fusion researchers actually exists.

327
00:21:29,420 --> 00:21:30,540
Let's pretend it's all real.

328
00:21:30,680 --> 00:21:39,320
Right. Even then, the scale gap between those microscopic energetic shifts and the macroscopic curvature of space-time is devastating.

329
00:21:39,320 --> 00:21:43,340
Devastating how. Walk me through the math of space-time curvature.

330
00:21:43,940 --> 00:21:48,440
So in Einstein's equations, energy density does act as a source term for gravity.

331
00:21:48,940 --> 00:21:55,900
Mass and energy are equivalent, so a highly energetic box is technically infinitesimally heavier than a cold box.

332
00:21:56,000 --> 00:21:56,720
Okay, that makes sense.

333
00:21:56,860 --> 00:22:00,120
But the stiffness of space-time is unimaginably high.

334
00:22:00,120 --> 00:22:05,220
It takes the mass of the entire Earth to create the 1g of gravity we feel right now.

335
00:22:05,820 --> 00:22:14,780
The energy density you can access in a laboratory benchtop cavity or even a localized nuclear reactor is orders of magnitude, like billions upon billions of times.

336
00:22:14,980 --> 00:22:18,400
Too small to register as a measurable change in gravitational mass.

337
00:22:18,460 --> 00:22:19,480
The math just isn't there.

338
00:22:19,480 --> 00:22:23,440
Not even close. You cannot point to a tabletop microwave cavity and say,

339
00:22:24,040 --> 00:22:27,140
I am manipulating vacuum energy, therefore I have built a warp drive.

340
00:22:27,340 --> 00:22:31,980
It is literally like splashing your hand in a bathtub and claiming you can redirect a tsunami.

341
00:22:32,140 --> 00:22:37,780
You're taking a real phenomenon, energy curving space, and stretching it until it just snaps.

342
00:22:38,500 --> 00:22:41,380
And we don't just see this in physics, right? We see it in fringe biology, too.

343
00:22:42,020 --> 00:22:44,700
I was totally fascinated by the section on Philip Callahan.

344
00:22:44,880 --> 00:22:46,380
Oh, the paramagnetic soil.

345
00:22:46,380 --> 00:22:53,760
Yes. He claimed that paramagnetic soil, which is just soil rich in iron-bearing minerals, acted as a cosmic antenna.

346
00:22:54,380 --> 00:22:57,820
He said it was channeling atmospheric energy to make plants grow faster.

347
00:22:58,420 --> 00:23:05,100
He even built these weird, ancient-looking Irish round towers on farms to supposedly focus this cosmic energy.

348
00:23:05,480 --> 00:23:09,660
Soil paramagnetism is a real, easily measurable physical property.

349
00:23:09,660 --> 00:23:17,100
Materials with unpaired electrons in their atomic structure will temporarily align their magnetic moments with an external magnetic field.

350
00:23:17,300 --> 00:23:18,420
Right. They respond to magnets.

351
00:23:18,640 --> 00:23:22,180
But the key word is respond. They respond weakly to existing fields.

352
00:23:22,680 --> 00:23:28,520
They do not act as antennas, they do not channel energy, and they certainly do not broadcast cosmic life force.

353
00:23:28,880 --> 00:23:32,040
So why were the farmers who listened to him getting better crops?

354
00:23:32,600 --> 00:23:35,760
Because they swore it worked. They were getting huge yields.

355
00:23:35,760 --> 00:23:46,900
Because of a completely mundane confound. The iron-rich minerals that exhibit strong paramagnetism, like basalt, they usually originate from ancient volcanic ash.

356
00:23:47,500 --> 00:23:48,400
Oh, oh I see.

357
00:23:48,460 --> 00:23:58,780
Yeah. Volcanic soil is naturally packed with highly bioavailable trace minerals, and its coarse particulate structure vastly improves soil, drainage, and aeration.

358
00:23:58,780 --> 00:24:00,260
So it's just really good soil.

359
00:24:00,500 --> 00:24:08,900
Exactly. The soil on those farms was incredibly fertile because it was volcanic, not because it was acting as a magnetic antenna for cosmic rays.

360
00:24:09,000 --> 00:24:09,780
That is hilarious.

361
00:24:10,200 --> 00:24:13,400
And Vlael Kazna-Kaev. This is another amazing story from the dossier.

362
00:24:13,720 --> 00:24:17,560
He was a Soviet researcher who claimed he had discovered mitogenetic radiation.

363
00:24:17,720 --> 00:24:18,940
Right. The six cells.

364
00:24:19,060 --> 00:24:23,380
Yeah. So he placed two sealed glass flasks of cell cultures next to each other.

365
00:24:23,380 --> 00:24:31,220
He would infect one flask with a deadly virus, and a few days later, the cells in the completely sealed neighboring flask would also get sick and die.

366
00:24:31,540 --> 00:24:36,400
He claimed they were transmitting disease via psychic biophotons passing through the glass.

367
00:24:36,640 --> 00:24:43,340
And again, ultra-weak biophoton emission is a real documented byproduct of cellular metabolism.

368
00:24:43,880 --> 00:24:50,440
When cells undergo extreme oxidative stress, they occasionally emit a photon as metabolic byproducts break down.

369
00:24:50,680 --> 00:24:51,520
So there are photons.

370
00:24:51,520 --> 00:24:59,720
Yes. But Kazna-Kaev's monumental claim that these sparse photons were transmitting complex viral information across a physical gap,

371
00:25:00,180 --> 00:25:05,180
while it failed to account for a massive, mundane compound, chemical, volatile compounds.

372
00:25:05,300 --> 00:25:06,800
Gases leaking between the flask.

373
00:25:06,940 --> 00:25:11,260
Exactly. His flasks were sealed with standard laboratory stoppers.

374
00:25:11,540 --> 00:25:12,640
They aren't perfectly airtight.

375
00:25:12,640 --> 00:25:19,140
But when later researchers and Western labs tried to replicate the experiment, they used hermetically sealed glass ampoules.

376
00:25:19,640 --> 00:25:23,240
They melted the glass shut so absolutely no gases could seep through.

377
00:25:23,460 --> 00:25:23,980
And what happened?

378
00:25:24,260 --> 00:25:28,000
When they did that, the mirror cytopathic effect completely vanished.

379
00:25:28,540 --> 00:25:36,900
The six cells were simply exhaling toxic chemical distress signals that seeped through Kazna-Kaev's porous stoppers and poisoned the neighboring flask.

380
00:25:36,900 --> 00:25:41,880
They were communicating through mundane chemical seepage, not quantum biophotons.

381
00:25:42,220 --> 00:25:48,560
Okay, so if we can't measure our way to free energy, and we can't scale up quantum effects to build a warp drive,

382
00:25:49,100 --> 00:25:51,480
what is left for the ambitious inventor?

383
00:25:52,180 --> 00:25:53,420
We turn to brute force.

384
00:25:53,520 --> 00:25:54,400
Brute force, yes.

385
00:25:54,460 --> 00:25:59,500
The inventors who decide to just cheat the universe's ultimate accountants, which are the laws of conservation.

386
00:25:59,500 --> 00:26:09,580
This brings us to the realm of closed system thrusters, devices that claim to generate forward thrust without expelling any mass or propellant out the back.

387
00:26:09,580 --> 00:26:17,400
Right. We are talking about things like the Dean Drive from the 1950s, the famous M Drive from the 2000s, the NASICA's superconducting thruster.

388
00:26:17,940 --> 00:26:26,160
They all claim that by spinning off-center weights or bouncing microwaves asymmetrically inside a copper cone or vibrating a magnet near a superconductor,

389
00:26:26,740 --> 00:26:28,640
they can push themselves forward in space.

390
00:26:28,640 --> 00:26:31,380
And the rule they are actively trying to break is absolute.

391
00:26:31,820 --> 00:26:34,600
A closed system cannot move its own center of mass.

392
00:26:35,200 --> 00:26:40,620
By Newton's third law, every internal force has an equal and opposite internal reaction force.

393
00:26:40,780 --> 00:26:44,180
So if I push on the dashboard of my car, the car doesn't move forward.

394
00:26:44,520 --> 00:26:48,880
Great. If you sit inside a cardboard box and push as hard as you can against the front wall,

395
00:26:49,220 --> 00:26:52,780
your feet are pushing backward on the floor with the exact same amount of force.

396
00:26:53,320 --> 00:26:57,440
The force is summed to exactly zero. You cannot push a car from the inside.

397
00:26:57,440 --> 00:27:00,680
But wait. The Dean Drive was patented.

398
00:27:01,180 --> 00:27:04,460
The M Drive was actually tested by NASA's Eagle Works Laboratory.

399
00:27:05,040 --> 00:27:09,900
And they put it on a highly sensitive torsion scale, and the scale showed thrust.

400
00:27:10,380 --> 00:27:11,280
The graph went up.

401
00:27:11,940 --> 00:27:15,340
How do you explain the thrust if the physics says it's strictly impossible?

402
00:27:15,340 --> 00:27:20,800
Friction and thermal expansion are the quiet, devastating explanations every single time.

403
00:27:21,480 --> 00:27:23,980
Let's look at mechanical devices like the Dean Drive.

404
00:27:24,400 --> 00:27:28,820
If you have an asymmetrical, violent vibration occurring inside a heavy box sitting on a table,

405
00:27:29,080 --> 00:27:31,860
the downward force of the box is constantly varying.

406
00:27:32,020 --> 00:27:32,680
Because it's shaking.

407
00:27:32,900 --> 00:27:36,600
Exactly. It gets temporarily lighter and heavier against the table.

408
00:27:37,080 --> 00:27:41,580
This varying normal force interacts with the static and kinetic friction of the tabletop.

409
00:27:41,580 --> 00:27:44,900
Meaning it slips forward when it's light, and it grips the table when it's heavy.

410
00:27:45,220 --> 00:27:47,900
Yes. It is a stick-slip friction drive.

411
00:27:48,460 --> 00:27:53,760
It is fundamentally no different than a vibrating cell phone skittering its way off the edge of a desk.

412
00:27:54,160 --> 00:27:56,860
In the vacuum of space, where there is no table to grip,

413
00:27:56,860 --> 00:28:00,480
it would just vibrate in place forever, going absolutely nowhere.

414
00:28:00,480 --> 00:28:02,660
And what about the NASA M-Drive tests?

415
00:28:03,560 --> 00:28:07,840
Well, as the isolation of these experiments improved, the thrust approached zero.

416
00:28:08,620 --> 00:28:15,660
A team of rigorous researchers at TU Dresden in Germany eventually tested the M-Drive in a state-of-the-art vacuum chamber.

417
00:28:16,120 --> 00:28:16,900
And what did they find?

418
00:28:17,120 --> 00:28:24,460
They discovered that the tiny micronewtons of thrust perfectly matched the thermal expansion of the copper mounting brackets holding the device.

419
00:28:24,460 --> 00:28:31,680
As the microwave cavity heated up, the metal physically expanded, warping the center of gravity and slightly tilting the torsion pendulum.

420
00:28:32,180 --> 00:28:36,400
It wasn't pushing against the quantum vacuum. The device was just bending under its own heat.

421
00:28:36,560 --> 00:28:39,800
I feel like I have to step in here and just play devil's advocate for a second.

422
00:28:40,400 --> 00:28:44,340
Because the romantic idea of science is that rules are meant to be broken.

423
00:28:44,740 --> 00:28:44,980
Right.

424
00:28:45,140 --> 00:28:48,440
Aren't conservation laws just historical rules of thumb?

425
00:28:49,000 --> 00:28:52,200
We thought Newton was the final word until Einstein came along.

426
00:28:52,200 --> 00:28:57,260
Why are physicists so violently defensive about the conservation of momentum?

427
00:28:57,460 --> 00:29:00,580
Why couldn't an M-Drive just be the next paradigm shift?

428
00:29:01,040 --> 00:29:02,900
That is a really profound question.

429
00:29:03,400 --> 00:29:10,420
And to answer it, we have to talk about Nother's theorem, which was formulated by the brilliant mathematician Emmy Noether in 1915.

430
00:29:11,160 --> 00:29:16,300
Albert Einstein actually relied on her mathematics to resolve issues in his own theory of general relativity.

431
00:29:16,600 --> 00:29:17,120
Wow, okay.

432
00:29:17,620 --> 00:29:19,060
Noether proved something astonishing.

433
00:29:19,060 --> 00:29:22,820
She proved that conservation laws are not just empirical rules of thumb.

434
00:29:23,220 --> 00:29:25,380
They are not just things we've noticed tend to happen.

435
00:29:25,860 --> 00:29:31,780
Conservation laws are direct, inescapable mathematical consequences of the symmetries of space and time.

436
00:29:31,940 --> 00:29:33,220
Unpack symmetry for me.

437
00:29:33,560 --> 00:29:35,660
What does that actually mean in a physical room?

438
00:29:35,980 --> 00:29:42,080
So, the conservation of momentum is mathematically identical to the translational symmetry of space.

439
00:29:42,080 --> 00:29:48,320
Translational symmetry means that the fundamental laws of physics do not change depending on where you stand in the universe.

440
00:29:48,760 --> 00:29:59,160
If you set up a billiards table in New York and strike the cue ball, the physics dictating how the balls scatter is identical to a billiards table set up in Tokyo or on the moon.

441
00:29:59,280 --> 00:30:01,120
Okay, that seems incredibly obvious.

442
00:30:01,580 --> 00:30:02,820
Space is just space.

443
00:30:02,820 --> 00:30:05,520
It seems obvious, but the implication is massive.

444
00:30:06,080 --> 00:30:11,660
Noether proved that because physics is the same here as it is there, momentum must be conserved.

445
00:30:11,820 --> 00:30:13,520
You cannot have one without the other.

446
00:30:13,720 --> 00:30:14,580
Oh, I see.

447
00:30:14,980 --> 00:30:22,920
Yeah, if you claim to have built a microwave cavity that breaks the conservation of momentum, you are not just saying you found a clever engineering loophole.

448
00:30:22,920 --> 00:30:27,440
You are fundamentally claiming that space itself is mathematically asymmetrical.

449
00:30:27,700 --> 00:30:33,280
You are claiming that the laws of physics are different at the narrow end of your copper cone than they are at the wide end.

450
00:30:33,700 --> 00:30:33,820
Wow.

451
00:30:34,060 --> 00:30:41,000
So, to say the M drive works, you have to prove that a billiards table plays differently depending on which side of the room you push it to.

452
00:30:41,000 --> 00:30:54,480
Exactly. To overturn a symmetry that has been confirmed from subatomic particle colliders all the way to the orbits of galaxies, all based on a microscopic measurement at the absolute noise floor of a thermal sensor in a laboratory.

453
00:30:55,240 --> 00:31:05,640
Well, it inverts the burden of proof entirely. The math of the universe is deeply intertwined. You cannot pull a single thread without unraveling the whole tapestry.

454
00:31:05,780 --> 00:31:10,760
And that mathematical rigidity applies to energy too, doesn't it? Let's look at magnetic motors.

455
00:31:11,680 --> 00:31:17,120
The Yildiz motor, the Perendiv motor, Staorn's Orbo, which we talked about at the very beginning of the deep dive.

456
00:31:17,180 --> 00:31:17,420
Yes.

457
00:31:17,840 --> 00:31:25,700
These inventors arrange rare earth magnets on a wheel, angled in such a way that they supposedly push each other in a continuous, never-ending circle.

458
00:31:25,700 --> 00:31:31,320
But static magnetic fields are conservative fields. This means they do zero network over a closed cycle.

459
00:31:31,920 --> 00:31:39,760
Whatever kinetic energy it takes to force two repelling magnets together is perfectly, exactly balanced by the energy you get back when they push apart.

460
00:31:39,920 --> 00:31:40,780
It cancels out.

461
00:31:40,780 --> 00:31:46,600
It does. You cannot arrange static magnets into a waterfall that flows downhill forever. Eventually, the water has to go back up.

462
00:31:46,600 --> 00:31:50,300
And that brings us back to Staorn's live public failure in London.

463
00:31:50,820 --> 00:31:55,680
It does. They claim to have bypassed the conservative nature of magnetic fields.

464
00:31:56,080 --> 00:32:02,020
They submitted to the scrutiny they asked for, and the universe's accountants remained gloriously undefeated.

465
00:32:02,020 --> 00:32:06,840
It is a stark reminder that geometry alone cannot create energy.

466
00:32:06,840 --> 00:32:12,360
But what about when the geometry does work? Because I want to talk about the Alcubierre warp drive.

467
00:32:12,360 --> 00:32:25,520
Miguel Alcubierre, a real theoretical physicist, published a peer-reviewed paper proving that Einstein's field equations theoretically allow for a bubble of space-time to contract in front of a ship and expand behind it.

468
00:32:25,720 --> 00:32:29,600
A literal warp drive that moves faster than light. That's real math.

469
00:32:29,600 --> 00:32:32,500
The math works, but we really have to understand how it works.

470
00:32:32,940 --> 00:32:35,720
General relativity is typically a forward-moving equation.

471
00:32:36,220 --> 00:32:41,700
You input a specific arrangement of matter and energy, and the equations tell you how space-time will curve in response.

472
00:32:41,960 --> 00:32:48,940
But what Alcubierre did, which is a completely valid exploratory mathematical exercise, by the way, was work the equations backwards.

473
00:32:49,080 --> 00:32:50,140
He reverse-engineered it.

474
00:32:50,140 --> 00:33:05,020
Yes. He started with the geometry he wanted, a moving warp bubble. He plugged that geometry into Einstein's equations, and then basically asked the math what kind of matter and energy distribution would be required to generate this specific shape.

475
00:33:05,240 --> 00:33:07,180
And the math actually gave him an answer.

476
00:33:07,340 --> 00:33:13,780
It did. The math said, sure, I can make that shape for you. Just bring me a Jupiter-sized sphere of negative energy.

477
00:33:13,860 --> 00:33:14,580
Negative energy.

478
00:33:14,580 --> 00:33:23,360
And that is the fatal flaw. It requires massive planetary amounts of negative energy density, which violates the weak energy condition of physics.

479
00:33:24,060 --> 00:33:29,200
Nature does not let you draw a blueprint of a house and then magically invent a new type of wood to build it.

480
00:33:29,360 --> 00:33:31,540
But haven't people updated his math since then?

481
00:33:31,540 --> 00:33:44,540
They have. But even highly optimized, modern revisions of the warp drive math still require macroscopic configurations of exotic matter that no known quantum or classical process can physically produce.

482
00:33:45,340 --> 00:33:51,060
The Alcubierre drive is a brilliantly solved equation that has been mistakenly embraced as an engineering blueprint.

483
00:33:51,060 --> 00:34:00,140
Okay, what about James Woodward's Mach-Effect thruster? Because that is heavily funded, and it's grounded in real relativity, not impossible exotic matter.

484
00:34:00,360 --> 00:34:05,700
Woodward's thruster is certainly more theoretically respectable than a permanent magnet motor.

485
00:34:05,700 --> 00:34:18,060
It relies on a fluctuating mass effect derived from Mach's principle, which is the philosophical idea that local inertia is determined by the gravitational interaction with all the distant matter in the rest of the universe.

486
00:34:18,060 --> 00:34:21,780
So the stars are literally pulling on us, creating our inertia.

487
00:34:21,780 --> 00:34:37,420
Loosely, yes. But to extract the macroscopic thrust magnitudes that Woodward claims from his piezoelectric crystals, you have to read Mach's principle incredibly aggressively in a mathematical framing that most working theoretical physicists reject.

488
00:34:37,420 --> 00:34:39,220
And does it actually work in the lab?

489
00:34:39,220 --> 00:34:53,220
More damningly, on an empirical level, just like the M-Drive, as the test setups get more rigorous and heavily shielded, the measured thrust tracks closely with thermal expansion and electromagnetic interference artifacts.

490
00:34:53,220 --> 00:34:56,320
Which perfectly transitions us into our next major question.

491
00:34:56,780 --> 00:35:07,060
If the measurements are flawed, the scales are wrong, and the physics explicitly forbid these devices, how do these experiments keep producing positive results in the lab for their inventors?

492
00:35:07,560 --> 00:35:09,560
Why do they genuinely believe it's working?

493
00:35:09,760 --> 00:35:09,880
Right.

494
00:35:10,020 --> 00:35:14,560
The answer lies in the epistemology of self-deception. We have to look at the observer.

495
00:35:14,560 --> 00:35:22,960
To truly understand how a brilliant mind can essentially hallucinate data, we have to look at the cautionary tale of N-rays.

496
00:35:23,220 --> 00:35:26,800
It is one of the most important moments in the history of the scientific method.

497
00:35:26,800 --> 00:35:33,820
This is my absolute favorite story in the entire dossier. Paint the picture for us. 1903, France.

498
00:35:34,640 --> 00:35:42,740
Prosper René Blondelot, a highly respected physicist, announces he has discovered a brand new form of radiation. He calls them N-rays.

499
00:35:42,880 --> 00:35:51,600
Blondelot was a giant in his field, too. He detected these N-rays by watching a faintly glowing phosphorescent thread in a completely darkened laboratory.

500
00:35:51,600 --> 00:35:59,360
He claimed that when he directed an invisible beam of N-rays at the thread using a special aluminum prism, the thread would glow slightly brighter.

501
00:35:59,680 --> 00:35:59,820
Okay.

502
00:35:59,940 --> 00:36:09,380
So he published his findings, and within a year, dozens of other prestigious French laboratories published their own peer-reviewed papers confirming they had also detected N-rays.

503
00:36:09,600 --> 00:36:15,100
So you have independent confirmation. Science is working exactly as it should. Multiple labs are seeing the exact same thing.

504
00:36:15,100 --> 00:36:22,800
It seemed perfect. Until an American physicist named Robert W. Wood traveled to France to visit Blondelot's laboratory.

505
00:36:23,780 --> 00:36:27,520
Wood sat in the pitch-black room while Blondelot and his assistant ran the experiment.

506
00:36:28,200 --> 00:36:37,400
The assistant was verbally calling out exactly when the thread got brighter and when it got dimmer, supposedly corresponding to when the N-rays were passing through the aluminum prism.

507
00:36:37,400 --> 00:36:40,240
And then Wood does something just absolutely ruthless.

508
00:36:40,820 --> 00:36:48,400
In the utter darkness of the lab, Wood quietly reaches out, grabs the crucial aluminum prism off the table, and slips it into his pocket.

509
00:36:48,700 --> 00:36:51,460
He entirely breaks the optical path of the machine.

510
00:36:51,620 --> 00:36:52,660
And what did the assistant do?

511
00:36:52,860 --> 00:36:56,640
The assistant continued to flawlessly call out the brightness changes.

512
00:36:57,300 --> 00:36:59,240
Ah, it is brighter now. It is dimmer now.

513
00:36:59,460 --> 00:37:03,620
He was narrating the effects of a prism that was currently sitting in an American's pocket.

514
00:37:03,760 --> 00:37:04,440
Oh, man.

515
00:37:04,440 --> 00:37:07,360
It was pure, unadulterated expectation bias.

516
00:37:07,740 --> 00:37:08,960
The N-rays never existed.

517
00:37:09,580 --> 00:37:13,020
The assistant was seeing what he intensely expected to see in a dark room.

518
00:37:13,320 --> 00:37:15,620
The screen went dark, metaphorically speaking.

519
00:37:16,680 --> 00:37:32,580
I love that story because it proves that independent confirmation by dozens of other labs is completely worthless if all those confirming labs are using the exact same flawed, highly subjective, expectation-vulnerable methodology.

520
00:37:32,580 --> 00:37:35,840
It is the ultimate proof that you must blind an experiment.

521
00:37:36,340 --> 00:37:40,780
If you don't control the environment and blind the observer, you aren't measuring the universe.

522
00:37:41,080 --> 00:37:42,720
You are just measuring your own psychology.

523
00:37:42,800 --> 00:37:46,380
Which is exactly what John Hutchison did in Canada, the famous Hutchison effect.

524
00:37:46,540 --> 00:37:50,800
A textbook example of an uncontrolled apparatus masquerading as a discovery.

525
00:37:51,560 --> 00:37:58,800
Hutchison basically filled a garage with unshielded Tesla coils, Van de Graaff generators, and massive radio frequency transmitters.

526
00:37:58,800 --> 00:38:01,300
And he essentially just turned them all on at once.

527
00:38:01,420 --> 00:38:03,140
Just a chaotic mess of energy.

528
00:38:03,220 --> 00:38:03,480
Yes.

529
00:38:03,960 --> 00:38:10,980
And he claimed he caught on video objects levitating, thick metal bars fracturing, and strange jelly-like transmutations of metal.

530
00:38:11,100 --> 00:38:13,160
But the catch was that it only worked sometimes.

531
00:38:14,160 --> 00:38:16,720
He could never reliably reproduce it for scientists.

532
00:38:16,720 --> 00:38:22,340
He blamed the ambient weather, or the power grid, or even his own personal mood on that specific day.

533
00:38:22,760 --> 00:38:29,560
Well, when you flood a small room with multiple overlapping sources of extreme, uncontrolled electromagnetic fields,

534
00:38:29,780 --> 00:38:37,880
you are going to generate incredibly complex standing waves, massive induced eddy currents, and violent arcing dielectric breakdowns.

535
00:38:38,300 --> 00:38:40,120
So the physics is real, just messy.

536
00:38:40,260 --> 00:38:40,780
Very messy.

537
00:38:40,780 --> 00:38:48,040
Eddy currents interacting with strong, ambient magnetic fields can absolutely move or violently throw small metal objects.

538
00:38:48,380 --> 00:38:51,020
Intense RF heating will melt or warp things.

539
00:38:51,440 --> 00:38:54,600
Uncontrolled, high-voltage arcing will fracture metal lattices.

540
00:38:55,020 --> 00:39:01,000
All of it is conventional, known physics, rendered completely chaotic by a terrible experimental setup.

541
00:39:01,120 --> 00:39:03,180
So when he couldn't repeat it, he just blamed the weather.

542
00:39:03,360 --> 00:39:03,600
Right.

543
00:39:03,600 --> 00:39:10,400
When an effect only works sporadically, and the inventor requires vague environmental sensitivity to excuse failures,

544
00:39:10,720 --> 00:39:14,440
it is the undeniable signature of an artifact, not a new discovery.

545
00:39:14,920 --> 00:39:18,860
We see that same failure to isolate variables with Nikolai Khozarev's mirrors.

546
00:39:19,680 --> 00:39:26,780
Khozarev was a Soviet astrophysicist who claimed you could mathematically focus time density using massive concave aluminum mirrors.

547
00:39:27,260 --> 00:39:32,880
He put biological samples and delicate instruments at the focal point of these mirrors and measured strange anomalous readings.

548
00:39:32,880 --> 00:39:37,120
We really have to step back and ask what a concave mirror actually is.

549
00:39:37,780 --> 00:39:40,540
It is a highly efficient conventional optical device.

550
00:39:41,100 --> 00:39:48,680
It perfectly focuses ambient heat, infrared radiation, light, and even acoustic room vibrations precisely at its focal point.

551
00:39:48,900 --> 00:39:50,880
It's just a magnifying glass for room noise.

552
00:39:51,000 --> 00:39:51,320
Yes.

553
00:39:51,700 --> 00:40:01,040
Of course, a delicate biological sample is going to react strangely when you unknowingly place it in an intense, invisible focal hotspot of ambient room energy.

554
00:40:01,040 --> 00:40:08,840
Furthermore, Khozarev circularly defined time density by the very thermal and biological effects it was supposedly causing.

555
00:40:09,340 --> 00:40:14,300
It became an unfalsifiable claim resting on a completely mundane optical confound.

556
00:40:14,400 --> 00:40:20,120
It's like setting off fireworks in a funhouse full of mirrors, pointing to a weird shadow, and claiming you've discovered a new dimension.

557
00:40:20,820 --> 00:40:23,120
And what about Alexander Ternetsky's plasma generator?

558
00:40:23,120 --> 00:40:28,340
He claimed his plasma discharge tube became self-sustaining and produced over-unity energy.

559
00:40:28,700 --> 00:40:36,340
Ternetsky fell victim to a phenomenon called negative differential resistance, which is incredibly common in gas discharge tubes.

560
00:40:37,120 --> 00:40:42,780
A tube of gas takes a massive high-voltage spike to initially ionize and ignite.

561
00:40:43,320 --> 00:40:48,580
But once the plasma is established, it can sustain that plasma at a significantly lower voltage.

562
00:40:48,700 --> 00:40:50,540
So it takes less juice to keep it going.

563
00:40:50,540 --> 00:40:58,240
Right. Ternetsky saw the required voltage dramatically drop on his meters and excitedly called the reaction self-sustaining.

564
00:40:58,460 --> 00:40:59,520
But it wasn't unplugged.

565
00:40:59,600 --> 00:41:07,580
Exactly. He completely ignored the fact that his biased circuit was still drawing continuous, heavy current from the wall to keep the plasma alive.

566
00:41:07,840 --> 00:41:13,120
It is the exact same underlying physics operating inside a mundane neon sign at a diner.

567
00:41:13,500 --> 00:41:17,920
Speaking of things that look like magic but are entirely mundane, the lifters.

568
00:41:17,920 --> 00:41:23,160
The Bifeld-Brown effect. If you have spent any time on YouTube in the early 2000s, you saw these.

569
00:41:23,200 --> 00:41:24,020
Oh, they were everywhere.

570
00:41:24,320 --> 00:41:30,240
They are these silent hovering triangles made of balsa wood, tin foil, and thin copper wire.

571
00:41:31,280 --> 00:41:35,780
You hook them up to a high-voltage supply and they float in the air with no moving parts.

572
00:41:36,560 --> 00:41:41,360
People swore up and down it was electrogravitic propulsion that high-voltage warps gravity.

573
00:41:41,360 --> 00:41:46,080
I will admit it is incredibly visually compelling. It looks exactly like silent anti-gravity.

574
00:41:46,500 --> 00:41:53,040
But the phenomenon is entirely electrohydrodynamic. It is a well-understood process called ionic wind.

575
00:41:53,360 --> 00:41:54,880
Ionic wind. How does that work?

576
00:41:54,880 --> 00:42:01,400
The extreme high-voltage ionizes the air molecules immediately surrounding the thin upper wire.

577
00:42:02,020 --> 00:42:07,180
Those charged ions are then violently accelerated downward toward the oppositely charged tinfoil skirt.

578
00:42:07,580 --> 00:42:15,480
As they speed downward, they collide with thousands of neutral air molecules, transferring their momentum and pushing a massive wash of air downward.

579
00:42:15,680 --> 00:42:17,900
So it's pushing air down, which pushes the craft up.

580
00:42:18,000 --> 00:42:22,440
By Newton's third law, yes. It is just a highly inefficient solid-state fan.

581
00:42:22,440 --> 00:42:24,900
And the ultimate, undeniable proof of this.

582
00:42:24,940 --> 00:42:27,980
Toot the lifter inside a vacuum chamber and pump the air out.

583
00:42:28,080 --> 00:42:28,980
And it drops like a stone.

584
00:42:29,400 --> 00:42:35,220
Exactly. Without an atmospheric medium to ionize and accelerate, there is absolutely zero thrust.

585
00:42:35,520 --> 00:42:38,620
It has absolutely no connection to gravity or space-time.

586
00:42:38,900 --> 00:42:49,140
So we've walked through flawed measurements, catastrophic misunderstandings of scale, blatant violations of conservation laws, and the psychology of expectation bias.

587
00:42:49,260 --> 00:42:50,040
A lot of pitfalls.

588
00:42:50,040 --> 00:42:57,120
It is. But what happens when the miraculous device can't even be tested in a vacuum chamber because it's conveniently missing?

589
00:42:57,920 --> 00:43:01,720
This brings us to the most seductive part of the entire fringe physics world.

590
00:43:02,280 --> 00:43:03,620
The mythology of suppression.

591
00:43:04,240 --> 00:43:06,600
The narrative of the persecuted genius.

592
00:43:06,780 --> 00:43:12,020
A mythology that centers almost entirely around one historical figure, Nikola Tesla.

593
00:43:12,760 --> 00:43:16,060
He has been elevated to a quasi-religious status on the internet.

594
00:43:16,060 --> 00:43:18,320
The patron saint of the garage inventor.

595
00:43:18,620 --> 00:43:19,640
The legend goes like this.

596
00:43:20,360 --> 00:43:28,560
Tesla built the massive Wardenclyffe Tower on Long Island to beam-free, unlimited, unminerable zero-point energy to the entire world.

597
00:43:29,060 --> 00:43:34,300
J.P. Morgan, his ruthless financier, panicked because he realized you couldn't put a meter on free energy.

598
00:43:34,460 --> 00:43:34,660
Right.

599
00:43:34,820 --> 00:43:40,380
So Morgan pulled the funding, destroyed the tower, and suppressed the technology to protect his copper wire monopolies.

600
00:43:40,380 --> 00:43:44,040
It is a phenomenal, emotionally resonant story.

601
00:43:44,420 --> 00:43:47,780
But the actual historical record is brutally mundane.

602
00:43:48,180 --> 00:43:54,700
If you actually read Tesla's patents for Wardenclyffe, he never once claimed to be generating free energy from the vacuum.

603
00:43:55,160 --> 00:43:55,500
Really?

604
00:43:55,500 --> 00:43:56,760
Never, never.

605
00:43:57,300 --> 00:44:11,440
The patents explicitly describe a highly efficient system to transmit conventionally generated electrical power, like the immense power being generated by the Niagara Falls hydroelectric plant, by pumping it into the earth and utilizing the planet's resonant frequencies.

606
00:44:11,960 --> 00:44:15,700
It was a transmission scheme, not a free energy source.

607
00:44:16,060 --> 00:44:18,820
So why did J.P. Morgan actually pull the plug then?

608
00:44:19,140 --> 00:44:22,960
Well, Morgan didn't fund Wardenclyffe to power the world out of charity.

609
00:44:22,960 --> 00:44:31,300
He funded it to compete in the highly lucrative race for wireless telegraphy, specifically sending financial messages across the Atlantic Ocean.

610
00:44:31,860 --> 00:44:45,660
But while Tesla was endlessly tinkering and building this massive, astronomically expensive tower, a younger rival named Guglielmo Marconi successfully sent a transatlantic radio signal using a system that was infinitely smaller, cheaper, and simpler.

611
00:44:45,880 --> 00:44:47,220
Tesla got scientifically scooped.

612
00:44:47,420 --> 00:44:50,900
He got scientifically scooped, and he got financially outmaneuvered.

613
00:44:50,900 --> 00:45:00,140
J.P. Morgan looked at the ledger, saw that Marconi was achieving the exact crucial goal for a fraction of the cost, and simply stopped throwing good money after bad.

614
00:45:00,620 --> 00:45:05,080
It was a ruthless business decision, yes, but it wasn't a physics suppression conspiracy.

615
00:45:05,340 --> 00:45:08,700
But what about the teleforce, the famous Tesla death ray?

616
00:45:09,020 --> 00:45:17,700
In his later years, Tesla claimed he had invented a directed particle beam that could shoot down 10,000 enemy planes from hundreds of miles away.

617
00:45:17,700 --> 00:45:23,040
And when he died in his hotel room in 1943, the U.S. government seized his papers.

618
00:45:23,960 --> 00:45:25,880
Surely they hid the blueprints in a vault.

619
00:45:26,300 --> 00:45:29,360
The teleforce was, sadly, a tragic press release.

620
00:45:29,900 --> 00:45:33,440
As Tesla aged, he fell into deep financial hardship and obscurity.

621
00:45:33,860 --> 00:45:40,920
He began making increasingly grandiose theatrical claims to the press on his birthdays just to attract attention and desperately needed funding.

622
00:45:41,340 --> 00:45:43,780
He never built a working prototype of the beam.

623
00:45:43,940 --> 00:45:45,760
But the government did take his papers.

624
00:45:45,760 --> 00:45:46,680
They did.

625
00:45:47,320 --> 00:45:51,180
The Office of Alien Property Custodian temporarily impounded his belongings.

626
00:45:51,940 --> 00:46:01,300
But that was a completely standard, legally mandated wartime procedure for the estate of a deceased immigrant who possessed advanced technical knowledge during World War II.

627
00:46:01,420 --> 00:46:02,920
They were just doing their due diligence.

628
00:46:03,120 --> 00:46:03,500
Exactly.

629
00:46:03,980 --> 00:46:07,720
And more importantly, those papers were fully returned to his family.

630
00:46:07,720 --> 00:46:13,300
They have sat in the archives of the Nikola Tesla Museum in Belgrade for decades.

631
00:46:13,900 --> 00:46:15,180
They have been digitized.

632
00:46:15,380 --> 00:46:17,900
They are freely available to international scholars.

633
00:46:18,240 --> 00:46:21,220
There are no secret death ray blueprints hidden in them.

634
00:46:21,340 --> 00:46:23,460
If there were, someone would have built it by now.

635
00:46:23,460 --> 00:46:24,840
Logically, yes.

636
00:46:24,840 --> 00:46:37,480
If the U.S. military had seized a working death ray in 1943, we really have to ask why no nation on Earth, despite trillions of dollars in defense spending over 80 years, has ever fielded a weapon matching his description.

637
00:46:37,820 --> 00:46:42,940
The suppression myth is just so much more exciting than the reality of an aging genius running out of money.

638
00:46:42,940 --> 00:46:46,560
And this trope of conveniently destroyed evidence is everywhere.

639
00:46:47,080 --> 00:46:48,040
Looks like a T. Henry Murray.

640
00:46:48,260 --> 00:46:50,560
Oh, the radiant energy device.

641
00:46:50,940 --> 00:46:51,140
Yeah.

642
00:46:51,460 --> 00:47:01,340
He claimed he built a radiant energy device in the 1930s that pulled kilowatts of power out of background cosmic rays using a mysterious germanium diode.

643
00:47:01,840 --> 00:47:07,740
But we can't test it today because he claimed it was smashed with a hammer by corporate saboteurs in 1939.

644
00:47:08,140 --> 00:47:10,760
Let's look at the physics of his claim before we look at the hammer.

645
00:47:10,760 --> 00:47:14,260
A germanium diode is an early, primitive semiconductor.

646
00:47:15,100 --> 00:47:18,560
It is used to rectify weak, high-frequency radio signals.

647
00:47:19,060 --> 00:47:24,060
It cannot physically extract more electrical power than the incoming signal inherently carried.

648
00:47:24,120 --> 00:47:25,140
And cosmic rays are weak.

649
00:47:25,280 --> 00:47:25,920
Very weak.

650
00:47:26,060 --> 00:47:30,700
Background cosmic radiation does exist, but it has an incredibly low energy density.

651
00:47:31,160 --> 00:47:36,800
To pull continuous kilowatts of power from background cosmic rays violates basic thermodynamics.

652
00:47:36,800 --> 00:47:40,400
It would be like trying to run a hydroelectric dam off the morning dew.

653
00:47:40,400 --> 00:47:40,740
Right.

654
00:47:40,940 --> 00:47:45,920
But because Moray claimed the machine was smashed and he conveniently never managed to build a second one,

655
00:47:46,080 --> 00:47:50,760
the destroyed prototype acts as a permanent shield against independent scientific testing.

656
00:47:51,080 --> 00:47:53,780
It places the evidence permanently out of reach.

657
00:47:54,280 --> 00:47:55,360
Same with the Papp engine.

658
00:47:56,200 --> 00:48:04,400
Joseph Papp claimed he built a revolutionary car engine powered by a sealed secret mixture of noble gases that supposedly never needed refueling.

659
00:48:04,400 --> 00:48:09,560
In 1975, he staged this massive public demonstration.

660
00:48:09,560 --> 00:48:15,320
He turned the engine on and it violently exploded, killing one observer and injuring several others.

661
00:48:15,820 --> 00:48:19,320
And Papp immediately claimed it was corporate sabotage by the oil industry.

662
00:48:19,700 --> 00:48:23,680
Noble gases, by their very chemical definition, are inert.

663
00:48:23,680 --> 00:48:24,980
They do not combust.

664
00:48:25,680 --> 00:48:32,400
To extract massive amounts of kinetic energy out of a sealed volume of noble gases at the temperatures and pressures of a standard engine block,

665
00:48:32,580 --> 00:48:35,140
you would require an active nuclear reaction.

666
00:48:35,280 --> 00:48:35,980
Which would be obvious.

667
00:48:36,140 --> 00:48:41,180
If that had happened, the explosion would have flooded the room with lethal, easily detectable radiation.

668
00:48:41,440 --> 00:48:42,240
That did not happen.

669
00:48:42,340 --> 00:48:43,560
So what actually blew up?

670
00:48:43,560 --> 00:48:51,640
What happened was a catastrophic overpressure failure of an uncertified sealed metal pressure vessel built by a reckless amateur.

671
00:48:52,080 --> 00:48:53,840
It wasn't an assassination by big oil.

672
00:48:54,000 --> 00:48:56,020
It was just a mundane boiler explosion.

673
00:48:56,020 --> 00:49:00,180
And then you step away from the tragedies and you just have the outright grifters.

674
00:49:01,180 --> 00:49:02,000
Otis T. Carr.

675
00:49:02,740 --> 00:49:07,860
He claimed Nikola Tesla personally taught him the secret of anti-gravity when he was a hotel clerk.

676
00:49:08,020 --> 00:49:08,920
Of course he did.

677
00:49:08,920 --> 00:49:16,800
He built a whole corporation around the OTC X-1, a supposedly functional flying saucer powered by counter-rotating metal discs.

678
00:49:17,240 --> 00:49:24,600
He aggressively sold stock and scheduled a massive, highly publicized public launch at an amusement park in 1959.

679
00:49:25,040 --> 00:49:25,920
And what happened?

680
00:49:26,700 --> 00:49:34,200
He repeatedly delayed the launch, citing sudden, unspecified technical difficulties before ultimately fleeing the scene and never showing up.

681
00:49:34,400 --> 00:49:38,900
Carr was eventually investigated, convicted, and went to federal prison for securities fraud.

682
00:49:39,480 --> 00:49:42,460
This is the phenomenon of the ever-receding horizon.

683
00:49:43,080 --> 00:49:46,100
The world-changing demonstration is always scheduled for tomorrow.

684
00:49:46,540 --> 00:49:47,600
Or Lester Hendershot.

685
00:49:47,600 --> 00:49:53,420
He built a fuel-less generator in the 1920s that was so convincing, Charles Lindbergh actually endorsed it.

686
00:49:53,780 --> 00:49:57,320
But when skeptical, independent investigators finally got a chance to look inside it,

687
00:49:57,380 --> 00:50:01,440
they found his complex magnetic coil was literally just acting as an antenna,

688
00:50:01,920 --> 00:50:07,140
picking up powerful local radio broadcasts and converting them to a tiny trickle of electricity.

689
00:50:07,600 --> 00:50:08,580
A literal radio?

690
00:50:08,580 --> 00:50:14,000
And when he tried to build a later version, they found a small battery secretly wired inside it.

691
00:50:14,120 --> 00:50:16,500
Which raises a critical psychological question.

692
00:50:16,940 --> 00:50:23,040
Why do these suppression stories survive and flourish for decades when the mundane, documented truth,

693
00:50:23,200 --> 00:50:26,920
like fraud, radio interference, financial ruin, boiler explosions,

694
00:50:26,920 --> 00:50:30,880
is right there in the historical record for anyone to read?

695
00:50:30,880 --> 00:50:35,920
I really think it's because a suppression narrative is deeply psychologically comforting to believers.

696
00:50:36,640 --> 00:50:41,100
It explains absolute failure through grand romantic villainy.

697
00:50:41,300 --> 00:50:44,300
It is much sexier and more ego-protecting to say,

698
00:50:44,660 --> 00:50:48,040
the men in black destroyed my world-changing machine than it is to say,

699
00:50:48,220 --> 00:50:52,240
I forgot to carry the one in my math equation, or I accidentally built a radio.

700
00:50:52,240 --> 00:50:57,780
It takes the very absence of evidence and flips it, making the absence itself the absolute proof of the conspiracy.

701
00:50:57,780 --> 00:50:59,480
That is exactly the mechanism.

702
00:50:59,480 --> 00:51:02,120
The lack of proof becomes the ultimate proof.

703
00:51:02,120 --> 00:51:06,260
Which brings us to the ultimate, extreme extension of the suppression myth.

704
00:51:06,940 --> 00:51:11,940
If human physics can't explain the device, and human governments are allegedly hiding the device,

705
00:51:12,380 --> 00:51:14,540
maybe alien physics can't explain it.

706
00:51:14,920 --> 00:51:21,180
We are now entering the territory of space aliens, secret agendas, and formalizing the untestable.

707
00:51:21,180 --> 00:51:24,660
We really have to address the UFO reverse engineering narrative.

708
00:51:25,080 --> 00:51:29,920
This was primarily popularized by Philip Corso's claims regarding the Roswell crash.

709
00:51:30,340 --> 00:51:35,900
The overarching narrative is that modern miracles like Kevlar, fiber optics, and integrated circuits

710
00:51:35,900 --> 00:51:41,680
were not invented by humans, but were reverse engineered from crashed extraterrestrial saucers.

711
00:51:41,940 --> 00:51:45,660
As someone who loves history, I find this incredibly insulting to human engineers.

712
00:51:45,660 --> 00:51:51,020
It is a staggering erasure of highly documented, decades-long human research and development.

713
00:51:51,540 --> 00:51:54,560
For every one of those technologies, we possess the lab notes.

714
00:51:54,980 --> 00:52:00,600
We have the iterative failures, the incremental hard-fought breakthroughs made by named human beings

715
00:52:00,600 --> 00:52:03,040
at institutions like Bell Labs and DuPont.

716
00:52:03,140 --> 00:52:03,860
We did the work.

717
00:52:04,100 --> 00:52:04,800
We did the work.

718
00:52:05,340 --> 00:52:09,940
Retroactively claiming it was alien technology is an unfalsifiable claim by design.

719
00:52:09,940 --> 00:52:15,100
You logically cannot prove that the government isn't hiding an alien saucer in an underground bunker,

720
00:52:15,300 --> 00:52:17,820
so the conspiracy loop permanently seals itself.

721
00:52:18,080 --> 00:52:18,900
And what about Bob Lazar?

722
00:52:18,900 --> 00:52:23,360
He is the man who single-handedly put Area 51 on the cultural map.

723
00:52:24,220 --> 00:52:29,620
In 1989, he claimed he was hired to work on captured alien saucers at a secret base called S-4.

724
00:52:30,160 --> 00:52:34,200
He said the ships were powered by a stable, super-heavy element called Element 115,

725
00:52:34,700 --> 00:52:37,900
which was bombarded with protons to generate gravity waves.

726
00:52:38,360 --> 00:52:40,640
Lazar's story was perfectly timed for 1989.

727
00:52:41,380 --> 00:52:45,000
The problem for Lazar is that humanity eventually caught up to his science fiction.

728
00:52:45,000 --> 00:52:49,360
Physicists actually synthesized Element 115 in 2003.

729
00:52:49,940 --> 00:52:52,300
We officially named it Moscovium.

730
00:52:52,880 --> 00:52:53,740
And how did it behave?

731
00:52:54,560 --> 00:52:57,980
It is intensely, violently radioactive and unstable.

732
00:52:58,200 --> 00:53:00,060
It decays in a matter of milliseconds.

733
00:53:00,560 --> 00:53:06,460
It is absolutely not the stable, machinable, handleable reactor fuel that Lazar's narrative strictly requires.

734
00:53:06,460 --> 00:53:07,860
And what about the gravity waves?

735
00:53:08,100 --> 00:53:09,500
Because we discovered those recently, too.

736
00:53:09,500 --> 00:53:11,700
We did, using the LIGO observatories.

737
00:53:12,280 --> 00:53:15,280
And what we learned is that gravity waves are incredibly weak,

738
00:53:15,620 --> 00:53:19,620
transient ripples in space-time caused by the most violent events in the cosmos,

739
00:53:19,820 --> 00:53:21,220
like two black holes colliding.

740
00:53:21,580 --> 00:53:26,140
They carry energy, but they do not exert localized, continuous thrust.

741
00:53:26,500 --> 00:53:30,000
They are entirely useless for propulsion at the scale of a spacecraft.

742
00:53:30,680 --> 00:53:35,700
But people want to believe so badly that they will fit any anomaly into the alien box.

743
00:53:35,700 --> 00:53:39,320
Look at the Kecksburg UFO incident in 1965.

744
00:53:40,240 --> 00:53:43,620
An acorn-shaped metallic object crashes in the Pennsylvania woods.

745
00:53:44,140 --> 00:53:49,320
The military immediately swoops in, cordons off the area, and hauls it away on a flatbed truck.

746
00:53:49,460 --> 00:53:49,700
Boom.

747
00:53:50,080 --> 00:53:51,320
It's a covered-up alien craft.

748
00:53:51,440 --> 00:53:58,320
Except the fireball in the sky perfectly matched the exact trajectory, velocity, and timing of the Soviet Cosmos 96 satellite,

749
00:53:58,680 --> 00:54:02,860
which had failed and was due to re-enter the atmosphere over North America that very night.

750
00:54:03,280 --> 00:54:04,260
And the acorn shape.

751
00:54:04,260 --> 00:54:08,640
The mysterious acorn shape that witnesses described is the standard, highly engineered,

752
00:54:08,800 --> 00:54:12,920
aerodynamic profile for 1960s-era Soviet re-entry heat shields.

753
00:54:13,200 --> 00:54:16,560
It was highly classified foreign space debris, not an alien scout ship.

754
00:54:16,900 --> 00:54:17,820
Or Dieglock.

755
00:54:18,240 --> 00:54:19,520
The infamous Nazi bell.

756
00:54:20,100 --> 00:54:26,960
An alleged World War II superweapon made of heavy rotating mercury that warped time and generated anti-gravity,

757
00:54:27,400 --> 00:54:29,200
supposedly hidden in a Polish mind.

758
00:54:29,200 --> 00:54:34,240
Dieglock rests entirely on the claims of a single Polish author, Igor Witkowski.

759
00:54:34,740 --> 00:54:41,200
He claimed in the late 1990s that he was shown a secret interrogation transcript by an unnamed intelligence officer.

760
00:54:41,760 --> 00:54:43,700
However, he wasn't allowed to make a copy.

761
00:54:44,120 --> 00:54:45,080
He didn't keep the document.

762
00:54:45,580 --> 00:54:47,360
And he cannot produce the officer.

763
00:54:47,360 --> 00:54:48,540
So there's no evidence.

764
00:54:48,980 --> 00:54:56,840
In the massively, exhaustively documented history of Nazi secret weapons, the V-2 rockets, the jet fighters, the nuclear program,

765
00:54:57,060 --> 00:54:59,940
there's absolutely zero corroborating evidence for the bell.

766
00:55:00,520 --> 00:55:04,380
It is a modern ghost story built on the aesthetic of rotating conductive fluids,

767
00:55:04,900 --> 00:55:08,220
which standard physics rigorously tells us do not produce anti-gravity.

768
00:55:08,220 --> 00:55:11,000
But wait, believers always point to the government paper trails.

769
00:55:11,640 --> 00:55:13,220
What about the famous Wilbert Smith memo?

770
00:55:13,660 --> 00:55:20,920
He was a Canadian government official who wrote a memo in 1950 stating that UFOs were the most highly classified subject in the United States government,

771
00:55:21,120 --> 00:55:22,440
higher even than the H-bomb.

772
00:55:22,660 --> 00:55:23,820
That is a real piece of paper.

773
00:55:24,040 --> 00:55:28,000
The piece of paper is real, but its context is wildly misrepresented.

774
00:55:28,820 --> 00:55:34,540
That memo was simply Smith summarizing his own private informal chat with an unnamed American official.

775
00:55:34,540 --> 00:55:39,380
It was not a confirmed official government finding or a policy document.

776
00:55:39,900 --> 00:55:44,460
In fact, Smith went on to run his own Canadian research program, Project Magnet,

777
00:55:44,540 --> 00:55:49,480
which spent years flying around trying to detect anomalous magnetic fields from UFOs.

778
00:55:49,540 --> 00:55:50,380
Did they find anything?

779
00:55:50,600 --> 00:55:54,540
They found absolutely nothing, and the Canadian government quietly shut the program down.

780
00:55:54,580 --> 00:55:56,640
Or Boeing's grass pea program.

781
00:55:56,840 --> 00:56:02,800
In the early 2000s, documents leaked showing that Boeing, one of the biggest aerospace contractors on Earth,

782
00:56:02,800 --> 00:56:05,300
was actively looking into anti-gravity.

783
00:56:05,440 --> 00:56:07,240
Gresenpree was a feasibility study.

784
00:56:07,640 --> 00:56:14,880
Large, multi-billion dollar aerospace companies routinely scout fringe technologies as a matter of due diligence hedging.

785
00:56:15,380 --> 00:56:17,420
They tasked a few engineers to look at the math.

786
00:56:17,820 --> 00:56:22,120
They looked at the claims, realized there was no physical mechanism or experimental evidence,

787
00:56:22,120 --> 00:56:26,580
and quietly closed the study without publishing a single patent or peer-reviewed paper.

788
00:56:27,160 --> 00:56:31,180
Conducting a preliminary feasibility study is not a scientific confirmation of the physics.

789
00:56:31,180 --> 00:56:35,060
Which perfectly brings us back to Salvatore Pace and his U.S. Navy patents.

790
00:56:35,360 --> 00:56:37,120
This always trips people up.

791
00:56:37,500 --> 00:56:41,900
Are you telling me that the United States government will officially file and grant a patent

792
00:56:41,900 --> 00:56:48,380
for a theoretical warp drive just to call dibs in case it ever accidentally turns out to be real?

793
00:56:48,640 --> 00:56:49,040
Yes.

794
00:56:49,460 --> 00:56:52,020
That is exactly documentably what happened.

795
00:56:52,220 --> 00:56:57,300
Internal U.S. Navy correspondence regarding the PANAS patents obtained via the Freedom of Information Act

796
00:56:57,300 --> 00:57:03,480
explicitly admits that the Navy's chief scientists had not verified Pace's inertial mass reduction physics.

797
00:57:04,040 --> 00:57:10,660
They actively pushed the patents through the patent office as a strategic legal hedge against Chinese aerospace advancements.

798
00:57:10,900 --> 00:57:12,220
They literally called dibs.

799
00:57:12,280 --> 00:57:13,280
It is a legal maneuver.

800
00:57:13,680 --> 00:57:16,100
And we really have to understand what a patent actually is.

801
00:57:16,100 --> 00:57:20,380
Patent examiners certify that an idea is novel, meaning nobody has submitted it before,

802
00:57:20,380 --> 00:57:23,580
and that the paperwork is technically enabled and filled out correctly.

803
00:57:24,100 --> 00:57:28,940
They do not build a prototype of the machine in the patent office to see if it violates thermodynamics.

804
00:57:29,560 --> 00:57:31,420
A patent is a legal claim to an idea.

805
00:57:31,620 --> 00:57:33,840
It is not a scientific confirmation of reality.

806
00:57:34,200 --> 00:57:37,720
It's like George Adamski, the famous 1950s UFO contactee.

807
00:57:37,720 --> 00:57:41,700
He claimed to have met blonde Venusians and photographed their scout ship.

808
00:57:41,700 --> 00:57:51,420
And the landing gear on his incredibly clear photograph of an alien ship perfectly dimensionally matched a 1950s commercial chicken brooder heat lamp.

809
00:57:51,720 --> 00:57:55,140
He literally took a picture of agricultural equipment and called it a UFO.

810
00:57:55,360 --> 00:57:55,780
He did.

811
00:57:55,780 --> 00:58:04,380
It perfectly summarizes the profound danger of taking claims or photographs or patents at face value without interrogating the underlying reality.

812
00:58:04,380 --> 00:58:04,900
Okay.

813
00:58:05,560 --> 00:58:10,260
As we reach the absolute bottom of Flyxion's dossier, we leave the garage inventors behind.

814
00:58:10,680 --> 00:58:19,360
We face the grand, overarching mathematical theories, frameworks so incredibly vast that they claim to explain everything in the universe and therefore practically explain nothing.

815
00:58:19,840 --> 00:58:25,120
This brings us to mathematical castles in the sky and the author's ultimate framework in tropic gravity.

816
00:58:25,120 --> 00:58:37,420
This is where we encounter incredibly dense theoretical models like torsion fields, which were heavily promoted by Russian physicists Gennady Shipov and Anatoly Akamov in the 1990s.

817
00:58:37,540 --> 00:58:48,820
They took a real, incredibly subtle mathematical concept from differential geometry, torsion, which describes the twisting of a geometric space, and claimed it was a physical field generated by spinning matter.

818
00:58:48,820 --> 00:58:56,520
They claimed this field could transmit complex information instantly across the universe without transferring any actual energy.

819
00:58:56,600 --> 00:59:02,180
Wait, stop. If a field transfers absolute zero energy, how can a scientist possibly measure it?

820
00:59:02,200 --> 00:59:04,000
You can't. That is the fatal flaw.

821
00:59:04,480 --> 00:59:10,300
If a field transfers zero energy, it physically cannot interact with any detector, biological, or mechanical.

822
00:59:10,620 --> 00:59:12,820
It is, by definition, utterly untestable.

823
00:59:12,820 --> 00:59:19,060
Shippov built a massive, mathematically complex, seven-dimensional framework to support this.

824
00:59:19,080 --> 00:59:19,540
Seven-dimensional?

825
00:59:19,740 --> 00:59:20,040
Yes.

826
00:59:20,720 --> 00:59:33,240
But a mathematical framework that is so flexible it can supposedly explain gravity control, telepathy, homeopathy, and instantaneous communication all at once is actually scientifically useless.

827
00:59:33,800 --> 00:59:37,820
If a theory doesn't explicitly rule anything out, it doesn't predict anything either.

828
00:59:37,820 --> 00:59:43,640
It ceases to be physics and becomes a vocabulary retrofitted to whatever miracle you want it to be.

829
00:59:44,000 --> 00:59:49,160
We see that exact same theoretical overreach with Randall, Mills, and his company, Brilliant Light Power.

830
00:59:49,680 --> 00:59:58,540
He claims he has discovered the hydrino, a state of hydrogen where the electron supposedly drops below its fundamental ground state, providing endless clean energy.

831
00:59:58,920 --> 01:00:03,040
The ground state of a hydrogen atom isn't just an empirical floor you can dig under with a shovel.

832
01:00:03,460 --> 01:00:07,060
It is a hard boundary condition dictated by the Schrodinger equation.

833
01:00:07,060 --> 01:00:18,400
Lowering the electron below the ground state is a mathematical impossibility, unless you are prepared to throw out the entirety of quantum mechanics, a theory that has been confirmed to billions of decimal points by modern technology.

834
01:00:18,560 --> 01:00:20,600
And have they ever produced a working device?

835
01:00:20,960 --> 01:00:21,280
Indeed.

836
01:00:21,420 --> 01:00:30,280
After 30 years and hundreds of millions of dollars in private funding, Mills' company has never produced a commercially available, independently verified device.

837
01:00:30,280 --> 01:00:31,520
Or Thomas Bearden.

838
01:00:32,020 --> 01:00:41,440
He wrote endless books on scalar electromagnetics, claiming Soviet scalar weapons were secretly causing earthquakes, and even triggered the Chernobyl disaster.

839
01:00:42,040 --> 01:00:49,720
Bearden constructed his entire worldview by misinterpreting a standard mathematical tool called gauge freedom in Maxwell's equations.

840
01:00:49,720 --> 01:00:58,180
In physics, gauge freedom is essentially a mathematical redundancy, a way to simplify the equations without changing the physical reality.

841
01:00:58,800 --> 01:01:03,640
Bearden treated this mathematical redundancy as if it were a hidden, physical, weaponized field.

842
01:01:04,100 --> 01:01:08,980
It is a fundamental misunderstanding of gauge theory, basically confusing the map for the territory.

843
01:01:08,980 --> 01:01:13,840
And this is where the author of our dossier, Flyxion, does something genuinely remarkable.

844
01:01:14,260 --> 01:01:18,880
After spending hundreds of pages dismantling everyone else, they turn their critical eye inward.

845
01:01:19,320 --> 01:01:24,500
They aggressively, meticulously debunk their own speculative ideas to prove that their rigor is symmetric.

846
01:01:24,500 --> 01:01:32,140
This is the philosophical climax of the document, and it's what separates a true scientific mindset from a believer's mindset.

847
01:01:32,660 --> 01:01:35,260
True scientific rigor must be applied symmetrically.

848
01:01:35,660 --> 01:01:41,260
You must be as absolutely brutal with your own cherished daydreams as you are with a grifter's schematic.

849
01:01:41,660 --> 01:01:43,940
Let me walk through a few of these because they are wild.

850
01:01:44,520 --> 01:01:47,420
Flyxion proposed a magnetic floor to propel a spaceship.

851
01:01:48,000 --> 01:01:50,000
They run the math and they debunk it themselves.

852
01:01:50,000 --> 01:01:57,360
They realize it violates Newton's third law of closed system momentum, making it identical to the failed Dean drive.

853
01:01:57,700 --> 01:01:57,740
Right.

854
01:01:58,060 --> 01:02:01,540
They proposed a future economy based on advanced mercury batteries.

855
01:02:01,980 --> 01:02:03,760
They audit the idea and debunk it.

856
01:02:04,340 --> 01:02:09,860
Mercury is horribly toxic, globally banned, and has terrible energy density compared to modern lithium.

857
01:02:10,480 --> 01:02:17,500
They even proposed replacing human skeletons with lightweight metal injected with high-pressure helium to make us buoyant and able to fly.

858
01:02:17,500 --> 01:02:22,480
And they dismantled that idea with a devastatingly basic magnitude check.

859
01:02:23,100 --> 01:02:29,680
To lift a human body in atmospheric air, you need roughly a cubic meter of helium per kilogram of mass.

860
01:02:30,020 --> 01:02:35,800
The tiny volume available inside a human skeleton wouldn't even offset a fraction of a percent of your body weight,

861
01:02:36,120 --> 01:02:40,360
let alone justifying the biological nightmare of surgically removing all your bone marrow.

862
01:02:40,560 --> 01:02:46,260
The only speculative idea of theirs that actually survives the self-audit is the solar O-Birth slingshot.

863
01:02:46,260 --> 01:02:53,680
It's the idea of doing a massive propulsive rocket burn incredibly close to the sun to gain massive exit speed.

864
01:02:54,120 --> 01:02:59,500
But even then, they humbly admit it's just solid aerospace math misapplied to interstellar distances.

865
01:02:59,920 --> 01:03:04,720
It would only get you to the outer edge of our solar system, not to Alpha Centauri in a human lifetime.

866
01:03:04,720 --> 01:03:08,080
But across all of these critiques, both of themselves and others,

867
01:03:08,500 --> 01:03:14,060
Flyxion uses a specific unifying theoretical lens to explain why gravity cannot be tamed.

868
01:03:14,460 --> 01:03:16,040
They call it entropic gravity.

869
01:03:16,200 --> 01:03:19,020
Okay, we've teased this all episode, well, all deep dive.

870
01:03:19,240 --> 01:03:20,740
Unpack entropic gravity for me.

871
01:03:20,820 --> 01:03:24,560
Entropic gravity proposes a radical shift in how we view the force.

872
01:03:25,380 --> 01:03:29,680
It suggests that gravity is not a fundamental local interaction like a magnetic field.

873
01:03:29,680 --> 01:03:36,880
You cannot just flip a switch with a spinning permanent magnet like David Hamill or Edward Leedskalnin at Coral Castle claimed to do

874
01:03:36,880 --> 01:03:39,900
and turn gravity off in a localized bubble.

875
01:03:40,700 --> 01:03:44,300
Instead, gravity is an emergent macroscopic phenomenon.

876
01:03:45,100 --> 01:03:48,760
It is the geometric bookkeeping of highly ordered configurations of mass

877
01:03:48,760 --> 01:03:52,260
and the massive redistribution of entropy across the universe.

878
01:03:52,460 --> 01:03:53,620
I really love this framing.

879
01:03:53,620 --> 01:03:57,300
If gravity is the macroeconomic GDP of the universe,

880
01:03:57,780 --> 01:04:00,760
these garage inventors are trying to crash the global economy

881
01:04:00,760 --> 01:04:03,860
by passing a single counterfeit penny in their basement.

882
01:04:04,100 --> 01:04:05,880
That is a brilliant way to conceptualize it.

883
01:04:06,240 --> 01:04:09,540
An electrical capacitor on a workbench, a spinning steel ball in a cup,

884
01:04:09,660 --> 01:04:12,260
a microwave cavity bouncing a few watts of power.

885
01:04:12,740 --> 01:04:18,640
These systems are simply too small by cosmologically vast orders of magnitude to ever touch that ledger.

886
01:04:18,720 --> 01:04:19,900
It's just a drop in the ocean.

887
01:04:20,260 --> 01:04:21,020
Not even a drop.

888
01:04:21,020 --> 01:04:26,140
The mass energy redistribution required to warp space-time and manipulate gravity is planetary.

889
01:04:26,720 --> 01:04:27,360
It is stellar.

890
01:04:27,740 --> 01:04:32,120
You absolutely cannot access that ledger with a benchtop apparatus plugged into a wall socket.

891
01:04:32,660 --> 01:04:35,760
Gravity doesn't have a local off switch because it is not a circuit.

892
01:04:35,960 --> 01:04:38,920
It is the fundamental accounting system of the cosmos itself.

893
01:04:39,180 --> 01:04:39,560
Wow.

894
01:04:40,140 --> 01:04:42,260
Okay, we have covered a staggering amount of ground today.

895
01:04:42,460 --> 01:04:47,460
We have traversed from the mundane, everyday reality of dead batteries and uncalibrated volt meters

896
01:04:47,460 --> 01:04:50,580
all the way to the wild heights of chicken-lamp spaceships.

897
01:04:50,580 --> 01:04:53,840
We have dismantled the tragic myth of the suppressed genius.

898
01:04:54,380 --> 01:04:58,600
We have seen how pure expectation bias creates literal glowing illusions in the dark.

899
01:04:59,000 --> 01:05:04,960
And we have proven that the universe's conservation laws remain gloriously mathematically undefeated.

900
01:05:04,960 --> 01:05:17,420
If we take one overarching lesson away from this entire dossier, it is that the immense gap between a compelling, romantic story and cold physical reality is bridged by one thing, strict, unyielding methodology.

901
01:05:17,420 --> 01:05:24,440
So I want to leave you with a final provocative thought, building directly on that beautiful idea of entropic gravity we just discussed.

902
01:05:25,180 --> 01:05:33,140
If gravity is simply the universe's macroscopic bookkeeping of entropy, the universe's relentless, unstoppable drive toward disorder and chaos,

903
01:05:33,480 --> 01:05:38,780
then the true free energy miracle isn't a secret zero-point machine hidden in a government vault.

904
01:05:38,780 --> 01:05:40,280
It's you.

905
01:05:40,500 --> 01:05:40,860
Yes.

906
01:05:40,860 --> 01:05:54,300
The fact that you, a human being, a highly localized, impossibly odored biological configuration, can actively resist the pull of entropy, maintain your cellular structure, and consciously observe the universe for decades,

907
01:05:54,300 --> 01:05:58,500
that is the most profound anti-entropic phenomena we will ever encounter.

908
01:05:59,200 --> 01:06:02,600
And the best part, it operates entirely within the laws of physics.

909
01:06:03,300 --> 01:06:05,340
The miracle isn't a human walking through a brick wall.

910
01:06:05,720 --> 01:06:09,580
The miracle is the structural integrity of the human hand reeking out to touch it.

911
01:06:09,840 --> 01:06:10,520
Beautifully said.

912
01:06:10,780 --> 01:06:11,680
So keep questioning.

913
01:06:11,980 --> 01:06:12,560
Keep testing.

914
01:06:13,400 --> 01:06:19,060
Remember that usually when we talk about a scientific measurement, the expectation of precision is there for a reason.

915
01:06:19,060 --> 01:06:26,680
Because the truth is often less about finding magic in the murkiness, and much more about just sitting down, blinding the experiment, and doing the math.

916
01:06:27,560 --> 01:06:29,180
Until next time, stay curious.

